s a terminal tile with no immediate meld potential and a higher unshown count (3), making it a safe discard. Retaining W3-4-5 preserves a potential concealed chow, aligning with the \"All Chows\" pattern (2 points) or other chow-based patterns. Other tiles like J3 or T4 are riskier to discard as they might be part of future melds or pairs.\nAnswer: Play B9"}
