s reduces the chance of opponents completing their hands while preserving terminal tiles (W1, W9) and B4 for potential future melds.\\nReason: Discarding F2 minimizes risk of aiding opponents, especially since the seat and prevailing wind are West (F3), making F2 irrelevant for wind-based scoring. Keeping terminals (W1, W9) and B4 maintains flexibility for terminal/honor combinations or potential chows.\\nAnswer: Play F2\"}"}
