he safest move because it's less likely to be taken, and if I get another T2, I can form a pair. So the answer would be Play T2.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The hand has five tiles (W1, W7, W9, T2, B4) and three existing chows. To complete the hand, a fourth meld and a pair are needed. The T2 is part of the T suit but cannot form a chow with the existing T3-T4-T5 meld. Playing T2 is safe as no one can chi it, and it allows waiting for another T2 to form a pair. Other tiles (W1, W7, W9, B4) are part of isolated sequences or could be used for risky chows with low probability.  \nReason: Playing T2 minimizes risk and preserves potential for forming a pair if another T2 is drawn or discarded.  \nAnswer: Play T2"}
